From: LYW-30M port <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spi-nand: force LYW RAM development NAND master read-only

This is a deliberate development-only guard. No writable storage images
are generated by the accompanying LYW profile. Only the separate NAND DTS chosen property permits writes;
the RAM profile still forces master and all partitions read-only.

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
@@ -1716,6 +1716,13 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* Development image: disallow writes through both master and partitions. */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("lingyan,lyw-30m") &&
+	    !of_property_read_bool(of_chosen, "lingyan,nand-writable")) {
+		mtd->flags &= ~MTD_WRITEABLE;
+		dev_info(&mem->spi->dev, "LYW RAM validation: NAND master forced read-only\n");
+	}
+
 	ret = mtd_device_register(mtd, NULL, 0);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_spinand_cleanup;
